# 11. One-Line Rule to Remember

> **Never assume** `address(0)` **means "not initialized." Check whether the initialization function itself can leave the checked value at** `address(0)`**.**

For lending protocols, always continue one step further:

> **Re-initialization → what trusted dependency changes → what can that dependency control → can it affect funds?**

